--TEST--
`Core\Db\Row::uint` answers zero and refuses the number below it, and the column it refuses still reads as `int`, so the floor belongs to the reader and not to the column — `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db\Row::uint
// The bound is asserted on both sides, one row apart: `0` is the last number
// this reader answers and `-1` is the first one it refuses. A reader stopping
// one number early prints plausibly against either half on its own.
//
// The same column is then read as `int`, which answers it. That is what makes
// the refusal a statement about the reader: the column is a whole number, and
// `-1` has no reading that is never negative.
use Core\Db\Row;

var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");
$db->execute(
    "create table counts (none bigint not null, below bigint not null, most bigint not null, missed bigint)",
    []
);
$db->execute(
    "insert into counts (none, below, most, missed) values (?, ?, ?, ?)",
    [0, -1, 9223372036854775807, null]
);

array<Row> $one = $db->query("select none, below, most, missed from counts", [])->all();
var $row = $one[0];

// The two ends this reader answers, and the one number past the floor.
array<string> $asked = ["none", "most", "below"];
foreach ($asked as string $column) {
    try {
        // The read comes first, so a refusal prints no half line before it.
        ?uint $answered = $row->uint($column);
        echo "uint over ", $column, ": ", $answered ?? 0, "\n";
    } catch (LogicError $stopped) {
        echo "uint over ", $column, ": refused\n";
    }
}

// The twin reader over the very same column, which answers it.
echo "int over below: ", $row->int("below") ?? 0, "\n";

// A NULL column is an absence and not a refusal — `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`, spec § 18.
?uint $missed = $row->uint("missed");
if ($missed == null) {
    echo "uint over missed: null\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
# § 3: a SQLite connection's file path comes from its config block, so
# `db.connect` covers it.
[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]

[db.main]
driver = "sqlite"
path = ":memory:"
--EXPECT--
uint over none: 0
uint over most: 9223372036854775807
uint over below: refused
int over below: -1
uint over missed: null
